<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 17:27:42 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Tête à tête</category><title>War in Iran 'jeopardises the Trump presidency', ex-Obama National Security Council member says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20260918-war-in-iran-jeopardises-the-trump-presidency-ex-obama-national-security-council-member-says</link><description>
In an interview with FRANCE 24, former Obama administration National Security Council member Charles Kupchan said the war in Iran "in many respects jeopardises the Trump presidency", calling it "yet another failed war of choice" that has driven up fuel and living costs ahead of the midterms. Trump's advisers "prize loyalty over fact", he added.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1f13023c-b375-11f1-9407-9ff5c3f464d4/w:1024/p:16x9/CHARLES-KUPCHAN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1f13023c-b375-11f1-9407-9ff5c3f464d4/w:1024/p:16x9/CHARLES-KUPCHAN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">47814bc2-b341-11f1-a8a1-6bc07350d0ec</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 17:01:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marc PERELMAN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>REPLAY: Zidane names first squad as France manager</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260918-replay-zidane-names-first-squad-as-france-manager</link><description>
Zinedine Zidane named his first squad since taking over from Didier Deschamps as head coach of the French man's football team Friday. His selection included five new players and but excluded former squad members Aurélien Tchouaméni and Khéphren Thuram. Kylian Mbappé has been named captain.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/788b5674-b380-11f1-8d08-47f1c44d1006/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260918-180102-183323-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/788b5674-b380-11f1-8d08-47f1c44d1006/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260918-180102-183323-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7e403080-b380-11f1-8bb4-618be78e6b1c</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 16:47:43 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The 51%</category><title>A Sydney Sweeney ad goes viral: Are we all just being played?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20260918-sydney-sweeney-ad-goes-viral-are-we-all-just-being-played</link><description>
Another Sydney Sweeney ad goes viral – this time promoting a sports betting application almost naked. The campaign sparked fury among female athletes who said it undermines decades of progress in women's sports. Yet is the outrage itself part of the overall marketing strategy and ‘feminist-baiting’ merely a tool to get clicks?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f9cc8146-b37a-11f1-b6e7-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/ENMG-THE-51-PERCENT-260918-2027-Ep-3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f9cc8146-b37a-11f1-b6e7-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/ENMG-THE-51-PERCENT-260918-2027-Ep-3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">13214f0a-b37b-11f1-bc74-2358946cfd38</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 16:27:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Annette YOUNG</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Sweden's centre-left leader Andersson tasked with forming government after election</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260918-sweden-s-centre-left-leader-andersson-tasked-with-forming-government-after-election</link><description>
Sweden's parliament speaker on Friday tasked opposition leader Magdalena Andersson with forming a government after an election gave the left-wing bloc a narrow majority, setting the stage for difficult coalition talks. Andersson, a former prime minister, must bridge deep differences between four parties, with the centre party ruling out a government that includes the left in cabinet.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/40e68e1e-b36c-11f1-b0a0-af2d0a26bd49/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-18T081854Z-1103190166-RC2JLNAQH6AJ-RTRMADP-3-SWEDEN-POLITICS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/40e68e1e-b36c-11f1-b0a0-af2d0a26bd49/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-18T081854Z-1103190166-RC2JLNAQH6AJ-RTRMADP-3-SWEDEN-POLITICS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">376ca71c-b374-11f1-9745-f7735b9d1ab1</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 16:01:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/40e68e1e-b36c-11f1-b0a0-af2d0a26bd49/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-18T081854Z-1103190166-RC2JLNAQH6AJ-RTRMADP-3-SWEDEN-POLITICS.jpg">© Christine Olsson, via Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Access Asia</category><title>AI safety: No, China will not hit the brakes</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20260918-ai-safety-no-china-will-not-hit-the-brakes</link><description>
A spate of warnings in recent days about the dangers of AI have sparked mixed reactions: from Donald Trump dismissing the fears as a hoax, to Beijing criticising calls for the US to block its advancement as fearmongering. As President Xi Jinping heads to Washington for talks, FRANCE 24's technology correspondent Peter O'Brien explains why the two superpowers are unlikely to forge binding agreements on AI regulation. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af94dcdc-b365-11f1-aac3-d16598924449/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-HAB-DEEPSEEK-ILLUSTR-BARITELLO-Sonia-transfer.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af94dcdc-b365-11f1-aac3-d16598924449/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-HAB-DEEPSEEK-ILLUSTR-BARITELLO-Sonia-transfer.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2e31701c-b296-11f1-9984-e9cb2938fd2e</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 15:40:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Yuka ROYER</dc:creator></item><item><category>arts24</category><title>Agnes Obel captures the cosmic feelings of motherhood</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260918-agnes-obel-captures-the-cosmic-feelings-of-motherhood</link><description>
Her new album ‘The Meaning of Flowers’ tackles much more than just flora, as the Danish musician and composer explores the sounds and sentiments of the very beginning of human life. She tells us about creating emotionally rich soundscapes that have often been used in film and television. We also discuss the Faustian pact that artists can find themselves in when it comes to balancing creative, personal and professional lives.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b8716730-b360-11f1-be2c-fb8321752947/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-6325717696aad35956a9a22-20285954.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b8716730-b360-11f1-be2c-fb8321752947/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-6325717696aad35956a9a22-20285954.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6acb96c0-b362-11f1-af9c-1311635871ca</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 15:25:04 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Olivia SALAZAR-WINSPEAR</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Air France bets on caviar and champagne to lure luxury flyers</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260918-air-france-bets-on-caviar-and-champagne-lure-luxury-flyers</link><description>
Air France is betting big on luxury to keep wealthy travellers spending with lavish servings of caviar and champagne in first-class cabins as soaring fuel costs and disrupted travel patterns squeeze airlines worldwide. The campaign seems to have paid off, with the Paris-based carrier saying that premium bookings and revenue have grown this year despite industry-wide higher fares.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3fcf45d4-716d-11f1-9619-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-848A2NQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3fcf45d4-716d-11f1-9619-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-848A2NQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5429d936-b36c-11f1-bf4b-4b62b5b57e4b</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 15:23:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3fcf45d4-716d-11f1-9619-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-848A2NQ.jpg">© Daniel Slim, AFP, Archives</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Talking Europe</category><title>We’re ideally placed to chair EU budget negotiations, says Irish Minister of State</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260918-we-re-ideally-placed-to-chair-eu-budget-negotiations-says-irish-minister-of-state</link><description>
Ireland is managing a jam-packed agenda as the current holder of the rotating presidency of the EU. We caught up with the country’s Minister of State for European Affairs, Thomas Byrne, who was in Strasbourg for the 2026 State of the Union speech and debate with EU Commission President Ursula von der Leyen. We discussed key points from that address, such as a proposed ban on social media access for children, which Ireland is keen to push forward with during its EU presidency.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ef4257bc-b282-11f1-86a5-07ed91e97eb2/w:1024/p:16x9/GI-BYRNE.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ef4257bc-b282-11f1-86a5-07ed91e97eb2/w:1024/p:16x9/GI-BYRNE.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f15d9d8a-b283-11f1-a98d-171d6308f1c7</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 15:17:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Armen GEORGIAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Talking Europe</category><title>Ursula von der Leyen’s sixth State of the Union speech: A grand sweep, but thin on details?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260918-ursula-von-der-leyen-s-sixth-state-of-the-union-speech-a-grand-sweep-but-thin-on-details</link><description>
In this episode, we debrief one of the key annual events in the EU calendar: the State of the Union speech. It was Ursula von der Leyen’s sixth such address as President of the European Commission, and the second State of the Union speech of her second mandate.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/59db29c6-b285-11f1-9214-d7a11ace016d/w:1024/p:16x9/XT-070396-0916-France24-Lobby-EM01-EN-PGM.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/59db29c6-b285-11f1-9214-d7a11ace016d/w:1024/p:16x9/XT-070396-0916-France24-Lobby-EM01-EN-PGM.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0fa59d04-b286-11f1-8df4-5f3b635e73df</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 15:17:36 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Armen GEORGIAN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Macron convenes French party leaders as soaring energy prices put focus on wars in Iran and Ukraine</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/macron-convenes-french-party-leaders-as-soaring-energy-prices-put-focus-on-wars-in-iran-and-ukraine</link><description>
Haxie Meyers-Belkin is pleased to welcome Renaud Foucart, Senior Lecturer in Economics at Lancaster University’s Management School in the UK. According to Foucart, France’s energy and economic crises expose a deeper collision between economic constraints, political accountability and an approaching presidential election. He interprets Emmanuel Macron’s rare Élysée meeting with party leaders over soaring energy prices as both an exercise in presidential legacy-building and an attempt to force prospective successors to confront high energy costs, rising borrowing costs, limited fiscal room and the radioactive pension reform.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2ef56f32-b36b-11f1-8eeb-fb8321752947/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260918-130817-131456-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2ef56f32-b36b-11f1-8eeb-fb8321752947/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260918-130817-131456-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">34af281e-b36b-11f1-a8e3-47ec9f8a9b58</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 14:26:28 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sport</category><title>France's new head coach Zidane unveils team line-up for Nations League matches</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20260918-france-new-head-coach-zidane-unveils-his-first-team-line-up-for-nations-league-matches-live</link><description>
France's newly appointed head coach of its national men's football team Zinedine Zidane unveiled his first line-up Friday, featuring five new players and excluding former squad members Aurélien Tchouaméni and Marcus Thuram. Star forward Kylian Mbappé has again been named captain. Watch the video replay of our live coverage of the announcement.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/efd46b0a-b365-11f1-949c-43e12873d6ea/w:1024/p:16x9/Zidane-Zinedine-bleus-france-liste.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/efd46b0a-b365-11f1-949c-43e12873d6ea/w:1024/p:16x9/Zidane-Zinedine-bleus-france-liste.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7e4fab2c-b368-11f1-81bc-87e7ed1b400d</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 14:25:26 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/efd46b0a-b365-11f1-949c-43e12873d6ea/w:1024/p:16x9/Zidane-Zinedine-bleus-france-liste.png">© Studio graphique FMM</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Macron addresses energy crisis, warns of 'hybrid attacks'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260918-macron-addresses-energy-crisis-warns-of-hybrid-attacks</link><description>
President Emmanuel Macron said Friday that France would convene a G7 meeting dedicated to energy in the weeks to come as fuel prices soar amid the US-Iran war. Speaking to the press after a meeting with party leaders over the energy crisis and international security, Macron also said he had ordered measures to protect France's critical infrastructure from increasing Russian "hybrid attacks".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/59dd24be-b367-11f1-bfba-af2d0a26bd49/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260918-153058-153332-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/59dd24be-b367-11f1-bfba-af2d0a26bd49/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260918-153058-153332-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5f04cd7a-b367-11f1-8336-e943dad362aa</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 13:53:50 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Gaza documentary sparks political storm, protests in Israel</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260918-gaza-documentary-sparks-political-storm-protests-in-israel</link><description>
The Israeli filmmakers behind the award-winning documentary "NAZA", which uses anonymous military sources to speak about Israel's widespread killing of civilians in Gaza, have been the subject of a wave of threats and intimidation in their home country, one that has even targeted their families. Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu has said he intends to introduce legislation aimed at revoking the citizenship of people who "defame IDF soldiers."
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7ed0896c-b364-11f1-b311-43e12873d6ea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260918-144811-145002-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7ed0896c-b364-11f1-b311-43e12873d6ea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260918-144811-145002-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">83d0b568-b364-11f1-9435-d1f3703fee0c</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 13:36:14 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ukraine strikes continue as polling stations open in Russia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260918-ukraine-strikes-continue-as-polling-stations-open-in-russia</link><description>
Russia and Ukraine traded strikes overnight as Russians prepared to vote in parliamentary elections in which the Kremlin's main party, United Russia, is poised to keep its grip on power, with the only party that criticised the war was removed from the ballot.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6d326dee-b362-11f1-aae4-994e92b1193e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260918-143858-144054-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6d326dee-b362-11f1-aae4-994e92b1193e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260918-143858-144054-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">72b9d54a-b362-11f1-aa1c-b9ab51d9fa2d</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 13:31:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US approves sale of F-35 fighter jets to Saudi Arabia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260918-us-approves-sale-of-f-35-fighter-jets-to-saudi-arabia</link><description>
The United States has approved a $24.3 billion sale of 48 F-35 stealth warplanes to Saudi Arabia, the State Department said Thursday, the kingdom's latest major arms purchase since the start of the Iran war. Saudi Arabia has been repeatedly targeted with drone and missile strikes by Tehran's forces since the United States and Israel launched their war against Iran in February, and has also been hit by Yemen's Iran-backed Houthi rebels.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/49bb9402-b363-11f1-9ebf-43e12873d6ea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260918-144551-144748-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/49bb9402-b363-11f1-9ebf-43e12873d6ea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260918-144551-144748-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">500cbb24-b363-11f1-aca1-e1a56fcc4f9d</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 13:29:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sport</category><title>Mbappé quits Nike after career-long partnership for Swiss sports brand On</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20260918-mbapp%C3%A9-quits-nike-after-career-long-partnership-swiss-sports-brand-on</link><description>
France captain Kylian Mbappé has signed with Swiss sportswear brand On, ending a partnership with Nike that began at the start of his career. The deal marks On’s entry into football, with the company also appointing France and Arsenal great Thierry Henry as its football director. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/26a5c2a2-89c5-11f1-9767-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C27E2QJ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/26a5c2a2-89c5-11f1-9767-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C27E2QJ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3a737786-b362-11f1-872c-53a10a0f670b</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 13:28:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/26a5c2a2-89c5-11f1-9767-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C27E2QJ.jpg">© Charly Triballeau, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>REPLAY: Macron orders plan to counter 'Russian hybrid attacks'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260918-replay-macron-orders-plan-to-counter-russian-hybrid-attacks</link><description>
President Emmanuel Macron on Friday said he had ordered measures to shield France's key infrastructure and defence industry sites from increasing Russian hybrid attacks. The announcement came as Macron spoke to the press after meeting in Paris with political party leaders to discuss recent developments in the international situation including the wars in the Middle East and Ukraine. Watch his press conference in full above.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/db9631cc-b361-11f1-bd52-43e12873d6ea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260918-135735-143050-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/db9631cc-b361-11f1-bd52-43e12873d6ea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260918-135735-143050-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e1050bec-b361-11f1-a9bf-63224dea7f17</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 13:15:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Russian elections: 'Even the facade of opposition has gone'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260918-russian-elections-even-the-facade-of-opposition-has-gone</link><description>
Russians on Friday began three days of voting in the country’s first wartime parliamentary election, which features virtually no opposition and is all but certain to secure the Kremlin’s political dominance. France 24's Douglas Herbert takes a closer look.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5b938200-b360-11f1-a086-994e92b1193e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260918-134048-134652-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5b938200-b360-11f1-a086-994e92b1193e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260918-134048-134652-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">610837bc-b360-11f1-bee9-95cac161b4a1</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 13:10:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><title>🔴 Macron orders plan to protect France critical infrastructure against 'Russian hybrid attacks'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260918-macron-orders-plan-to-protect-france-critical-infrastructure-against-russian-hybrid-attacks</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">ee1eb63a-b35b-11f1-af42-31fb72e0081a</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 12:24:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Macron orders plan to protect France's critical infrastructure against 'Russian hybrid attacks'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260918-macron-orders-plan-to-protect-france-critical-infrastructure-against-russian-hybrid-attacks</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron on Friday said he had ordered measures to protect France's critical infrastructure and defence industry sites from "Russian hybrid attacks", adding that the threat from Moscow had intensified in recent weeks. 
